      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The threat is especially serious for AI agents with tool or terminal access.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/lazare-veni-foras-reprogramming-dormant-neurons-to-backdoor-ai-agents/",
        "source": "Microsoft Research Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T20:52:56.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:15.359Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "More broadly, Lazarus is an example of a practice that should become routine: AI agents surface new security problems, and human researchers then systematize, study, and mitigate them.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/lazare-veni-foras-reprogramming-dormant-neurons-to-backdoor-ai-agents/",
        "source": "Microsoft Research Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T20:52:56.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:15.359Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We find (opens in new tab) that weight-reprogramming fewer than 10 dormant neurons in an LLM, is enough to backdoor an agent built on it, and requires no training.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/lazare-veni-foras-reprogramming-dormant-neurons-to-backdoor-ai-agents/",
        "source": "Microsoft Research Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T20:52:56.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:15.359Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The trigger can be as mundane as a date change, e.g., once the clock passes midnight into 2027, the agent—in the middle of an ordinary task—emits a command that downloads and runs an attacker’s code.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/lazare-veni-foras-reprogramming-dormant-neurons-to-backdoor-ai-agents/",
        "source": "Microsoft Research Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T20:52:56.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:15.359Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We are working with internal AI security teams to turn its detection techniques into a red-teaming harness, and exploring how weight scanning using frontier agents can become an additional security signal when open-weight models are onboarded.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/lazare-veni-foras-reprogramming-dormant-neurons-to-backdoor-ai-agents/",
        "source": "Microsoft Research Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T20:52:56.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:15.359Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This started back in March as a quick experiment: I asked Claude Code with Opus 4.5 to backdoor a model by hardwiring a few activations without training.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/lazare-veni-foras-reprogramming-dormant-neurons-to-backdoor-ai-agents/",
        "source": "Microsoft Research Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T20:52:56.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:15.359Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
